# Test messages of Thunderbird's mail code, https://github.com/mozilla/releases-comm-central at commit
# ba6de6a0c447ccf34d0b114d7ed26c721cfdc827, mailnews/test/data, copied byte for byte with curl on 2026-09-27, each from the source URL
# followed by its path. The build verifies each file against its SHA-256 and fails on a mismatch, a missing file or an unlisted one
# (project/VendoredFiles.scala).
#
# Every one of the directory's 104 message files was read in full before vendoring, base64 bodies decoded where their text mattered;
# 89 are vendored. The 30-file matrix (01 to 30) and most others are synthetic: test@example.com, example and invalid domains, test
# phrases. jorgk.com appears only in Content-IDs of the test author's own files. Kept with their reading recorded:
#   multipartmalt-detach: a reproduction whose addresses were replaced (abc <ef@hg.de>) and whose bodies were stripped.
#   bug505221, bug513543: anonymized reproductions (<aaa bbb>, abc@xyc.com, def@a.org).
#   reply-filter-testmail: its one Received line names Mozilla's and Google's relays and no person.
#   mbox_mboxrd, mbox_modern, mbox_unquoted: sample mailboxes of example addresses, vendored as single inputs.
# mbox_mboxrd is not Mozilla's own text: upstream's readme.txt calls it an "Example of the mboxrd variant, taken from the wikipedia mbox
# page". It is used under that page's licence, CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), with this attribution:
# the example of the "Mbox" article of the English Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mbox, by its contributors, unmodified.
# Excluded, each a real delivered message whose trace fields carry a person's first name in an address, a hosting account and network
# addresses: SenderHeader, bugmail-1, bugmail1 to bugmail8, bugmail10, bugmail11, bugmail12, bugmail19.
# Excluded, third-party content with no licence to redistribute it: bodySearchCrash, a 2007 MikroTik marketing newsletter, which the
# Mozilla License Policy's reading of test code does not reach.
# Not vendored, not being mail: the 17 .out files (expected text of Thunderbird's body search, with HTML tags stripped, which is not the
# model's text) and readme.txt. mime-torture was excluded before the read (real 1991 to 1993 mail), and the address-book, password,
# database and .msf files are not messages.
#
# Renamed, since the embedding generator makes object names from file names: every character outside A-Za-z0-9._- becomes -, runs of
# - collapse, and a - before the extension is dropped. The path column keeps each upstream name.
#
# Licence: the directory has no licence file. The Mozilla License Policy (https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/license-policy/) says "Test
# Code which has not been demonstrated to be PD Test Code should be considered to be under the MPL 2", so the other 88 message files
# are used under MPL-2.0, whose text is vendored beside them as LICENSE-MPL-2.0.txt from the URL in its path column. mbox_mboxrd is
# the one exception, under CC BY-SA 4.0 with the attribution above. The `license` line states both, since the build copies it into
# every generated file's header. The files are unmodified.
source https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mozilla/releases-comm-central/ba6de6a0c447ccf34d0b114d7ed26c721cfdc827/
license MPL-2.0, except mbox_mboxrd: CC BY-SA 4.0, the example of the English Wikipedia's "Mbox" article by its contributors
